                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "7.5/10\nA fairly good and reasonably priced top down Serious Sam indie spin off. \nFor what it costs, you get a 9 level story campaign with large levels, 4 survival mode maps, co-op suport and a randomized mode. \nFor the most part levels do feel like they belong in a main game, being a mix of traditional corridor shooter flow with large arenas for big waves. The shooting and weapons all feel like they should and most of the classic enemies are here with some new ones. There's plenty of new lines for Sam, all delivered by his usual voice actor, so not only is the action plentiful, but it retains the charm of the main series. There's even a good soundtrack to go with it.\nThat said there are a few major draw backs that held it back from being great. The first are the mines. I don't know what they were thinking with this, but throughout some of the levels are these mine fields that will slow progress to a crawl and break the flow. Only way to deal with them is to get close enough to reveal them with out stepping on them, then shooting them while rolling away, because if you don't you will take damage. Thankfully, there is a mod in the workshop that makes them less annoying. The other is the lives system combined with checkpoints that are far between with no manual saves. This makes the harder difficulties more trouble than they are worth and Serious is borderline unfair. I strongly recommend sticking to normal for a first playthrough. The visuals aren't the greatest either, but they aren't bad like say... random encounter.\nStill, despite its flaws it is a pretty good time and the best Indie spin off. Shame it doesn't look like it sold well as I would have been up for a sequel.",
